// Code signing for local builds of Nook.
//
// By default Nook is signed ad hoc ("-"), so it builds without an Apple account. An ad-hoc signature changes with every
// build, though, and macOS then treats each build as a new app: Keychain access and privacy permissions are asked for
// again. With a stable identity (a free "Apple Development" certificate) they are asked once.
//
// Config/local-signing.sh runs before every `xcodegen` and writes Signing.local.xcconfig (not in git) with your team
// when an Apple Development certificate is in your keychain. Without one it creates a self-signed "Nook Local Signing"
// identity once and sets NOOK_LOCAL_SIGNING_IDENTITY, which the scheme's post-build action (Config/resign-local.sh)
// re-signs every build with. You can also write that file yourself.
CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = -
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =
NOOK_LOCAL_SIGNING_IDENTITY =

#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"
